  "notes": [
    "USB low-speed IN responder (docs/extension-study.md section 7.3): D+ on pin 0, D- on pin 1 (the pair pin), 50 MHz clock, bit time P = 16 with fraction 171/256 (33.34 cycles, rate -78 ppm).",
    "It receives a token (NRZI, stuffing after six 1s, end on SE0), checks the CRC5 residue 0x06 (preset 0) and PID = IN (0x69), waits for J after the EOP and, 95 cycles after that edge, sends the 3 queued words: SYNC+PID (16 bits, e.g. 0x4B80 for DATA1), then 8 data bytes; CRC16 (preset 1, init 0xFFFF, complemented) is computed by the unit. EOP: SE0 for 64 cycles, then J for 31 cycles, then the pins are released (the pull-up holds J).",
    "Packet level only: enumeration needs host service between transactions (docs/extension-study.md R1).",
    "Needs the line unit (options.line_unit rec16, docs/extension.md); assemble with --variant configs/variants/diet8_rec16.json."
